; AI board review of the executable core frequency-lift dictionary seed.
; The Form-native review flow persists each response before collection.
import "../form/form-stdlib/core.fk"
import "review-panel.fk"
import "review-ask.fk"

(ra-review
  "docs/coherence-substrate/core-frequency-lift-dictionary.md"
  "Review this executable seed adversarially and independently; do not edit any file. Read cognition/core-frequency-lift-dictionary.fk and cognition/tests/core-frequency-lift-dictionary-band.fk as the actual implementation. The intent is to preserve every observed sense while offering an explicit trust/sovereignty/vitality generation recipe for inherited control- or fear-bearing usages. Test whether the design truly avoids censorship, euphemism, compulsory positivity, English identity, semantic collapse, and false claims about word frequency. Test the definition of safety as trusted becoming, and every one of the 16 seed mappings. Distinguish what the native 65535 band proves from what is still fixture-authored or pending. Return PASS, REVISE, or BLOCK; name the strongest correction; identify any harmful or meaning-losing lift; propose a better architecture or vocabulary where needed; state what should be implemented as a coherent next movement; and preserve the governing premise that context—not a banned-word table—selects meaning and expression.")
